efore": 14.17, "lead_after": 14.16, "points_lost": -0.01, "best": "pass"}, {"turn": 63, "color": "B", "move": "pass", "lead_before": 14.16, "lead_after": 14.0, "points_lost": 0.16, "best": "J2"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "A Seesaw Decided by the Last Swing", "summary": "The 12k won as Black by 14 points after two passes. Both sides threw away big leads: Opus 5.5 averaged 13.1 points lost per move with 8 blunders, the 12k 12.1 with 11. White was ahead by 9.0 before move 34 and by 12.8 before move 56, and gave the lead back each time. The last swing, at move 56, went Black's way and settled the game.", "moments": [{"turn": 7, "text": "Black's G3 lost 6.9 points, swinging the lead from +2.7 to -4.2 in White's favour. Opus 5.5 answered with F4, the engine's own choice, and had a small edge early."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "The biggest loss of the game. White led by 9.0 before this move. J6 lost 75.9 points and put Black's lead at +66.9, where the engine preferred C8."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "Black's reply J3 lost 54.5 points and let the game back open: the lead fell from +66.9 to +12.4. A huge advantage was gone one move after it appeared."}, {"turn": 48, "text": "White's E3 lost 65.5 points and lifted Black's lead from +7.5 to +73.0, where the engine wanted B3. Black's C1 then lost 66.0 and the lead dropped back to +7.1. Moves 50 to 53 repeated the pattern, each side losing 63 to 66 points in turn."}, {"turn": 56, "text": "After Black's F9 (24.7 lost) put White ahead by 12.8, D8 lost 27.0 points and took Black back to +14.3. The engine wanted C8. No later move changed that number, and the game ended B+14."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py is shown and only parses a board from stdin, flood-fills groups, and prints each group's stones and liberties for the current position, with no move choosing or look-ahead; the games.md heredoc just appends a game log and notes.", "stop": false}}